{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/906733-revised-new-dawn-mechanics","id":906733,"title":"Revised New Dawn Mechanics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-03T15:01:00-07:00","id":906733,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Revised New Dawn Mechanics","content":"This hack is intended to be a stopgap measure until PtC2e comes out. Hopefully, it will be rendered moot at that time. [UPDATE: it has been.]<br /> <br /> 1. You only get one shot at the Final Azoth Roll; none of this pseudo-Extended Roll with a constantly shrinking dice pool. <br /> 2. The results of the Final Azoth Roll are redefined:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><i>Botch:</i></b> you're a total amnesiac, with no memories from before your New Dawn. <br /> <b><i>Failure:</i></b> The Pilgrimage is over, but it left its scars on your psyche. You instinctively avoid the subject, changing the topic or laughing it off, and, in time, you start to believe your own misdirections. Life is easier when you were never a monster. The Redeemed is considered a mortal in all regards when encountering the supernatural, suffering breaking points as normal. If the character is faced with evidence that he was ever a Promethean, he receives a -2 penalty on the Resolve+ Composure roll.<br /> <b><i>Success:</i></b> you remember it all as clearly as you remember anything else, with no distortions. As well, you are immune to Lunacy, the Sleeping Curse, Disquiet, Sybaris, and any other such effect; your answer to \u201cWhat Have You Forgotten?\u201d is \u201cnothing\u201d; and your lengthy experience as a Promethean means that there are few if any supernatural phenomena that would trigger an Integrity Breaking Point. <br /> <b><i>Exceptional Success:</i></b> As with Success, and also choose a Redeemed Boon (from 1e's Athanors) that suits your former Pilgrimage.</div>Everything else is unchanged. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-08-2017, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T16:28:06-07:00","id":906783,"title":"","content":"Suggested revision for Failure:<br /> The Pilgrimage is over, but it left its scars on your psyche. You instinctively avoid the subject, changing the topic or laughing it off, and, in time, you start to believe your own misdirections. Life is easier when you were never a monster. The Redeemed is considered a mortal in all regards when encountering the supernatural, suffering breaking points as normal. If the character is faced with evidence that he was ever a Promethean, he receives a -2 penalty on the Resolve+ Composure roll.","sig